.TH voltkit-gpu 1  "Voltkit 0.9.2" "Voltkit Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
voltkit\-gpu \- Monitor NVIDIA, AMD and Intel graphics cards and tune their power, fans, clocks and temperature
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvoltkit gpu\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Monitor NVIDIA, AMD and Intel graphics cards and tune their power, fans, clocks and temperature
.PP
Without a subcommand, shows each card with its readings and which controls it supports, with the reason for any it doesn\*(Aqt. Changing settings needs administrator rights, and anything you don\*(Aqt confirm is undone.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu show\fR
Show the graphics cards, their readings and what each lets you control
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu apply [\-\-save] [\-\-yes] [\-\-confirm]\fR
Apply GPU settings from a JSON file, undoing them unless you confirm

The file holds the settings for one card: its PCI address as "gpu", and any of "power_limit_w", "fan" ({"mode":"auto"}, {"mode":"fixed","speed_pct":50} or {"mode":"curve","points":[...]}), "temperature_target_c", "core_offset_mhz", "mem_offset_mhz", "voltage_offset_mv", and for Intel "core_clock_min_mhz" and "core_clock_max_mhz". Values the card doesn\*(Aqt allow are refused.
.RS
\fB\-\-save\fR: Keep the settings after a restart, and run fan curves in the background service
.RE
.RS
\fB\-\-yes\fR: Keep the settings without asking for confirmation
.RE
.RS
\fB\-\-confirm\fR: Seconds to wait for confirmation before undoing the change
.RE
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu forget\fR
Remove a card\*(Aqs saved settings and give its fans back to the card
.TP
\fBvoltkit gpu service\fR
Run the background service that applies saved GPU settings and follows fan curves
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
